# (HELMS forge-fix i2) begin (forge fix 2, the owner: "onion helms look alike at 1x; make the variants bolder"): `when
# helmfam-onion,<mass>` replace views, one bold outline per body-mass class (the first replacing view that holds wins).
# the kulah: a low pointed dome on a rim, mail hanging at the cheeks and the nape, the finial on its point (none, round,
# broad and mantle; tall and drop keep the base bulb). It stands 3 rows lower than the bulb (the run atlas, B10).
# Written by the HELMS area tools/d2.py (D R drawn; U is D with the face details dropped; L is R mirrored and re-lit).
# the kulah (none, round, broad, mantle)
# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r2, tools2/brass.py) A1-A3: on a dark sheen (the antique brasses) this outline takes a metal shading: a narrow lit band and specular streak, the mid-step body, a shadowed quarter, a glint on the brim's lip
view D key rest origin 2 4 when helmfam-onion,variant-1,sheen-dark replace
mark crown 9 0
mark socket 9 0
